(a) Members. The ethics committee shall consist of three members. The mayor will appoint one member, the council shall appoint one member and the third member shall be appointed by the two members appointed by the mayor and council. One member of the committee should be an attorney in good standing with the state bar. The city attorney shall act as legal counsel to the committee, and shall cast no vote on any subject, which comes before the committee. At any meeting of the committee two members shall constitute a quorum. The committee shall elect one of the members as chairperson. The chairperson may vote on any matter that comes before the committee where no conflict exists. The members shall be designated member one, member two and member three only for purposes of staggering their terms of service. Each member of the ethics committee shall be a resident of the city and shall remain a resident of the city while serving as a member of the ethics committee. No person shall serve as a member of the ethics committee if the person has or has had within the preceding one-year period, any interest in any contract, transaction, or official action of the city. The members of the ethics committee shall serve staggered four-year terms after the terms of the original members are completed. Starting on January 1, 2009, member one's term shall end. The term of member two shall end on January 1, 2010. The term of member three shall end on January 1, 2011. The four-year terms of future committee members shall thereafter continue as staggered. The members of the ethics committee shall serve without compensation. However, travel and other expenses incurred on behalf of the city may be repaid. The mayor and council of the city shall provide meeting space for the ethics committee. Subject to budgetary procedures and requirements of the city, the city shall provide the ethics committee with such supplies and equipment as may be reasonably necessary for it to perform its duties and responsibilities.
(b) Criminal background check. Prior to taking office, candidates for the ethics committee must agree to undergo a criminal background check conducted by the police department prior to designation, the results of which will be forwarded to the mayor and council. Upon appointment each individual shall attend a training session on the code of ethics conducted by the city.
(c) Duties and powers. The constituted ethics committee shall have the following duties and powers:
(1) To establish procedures, rules and regulations governing its internal organization and conduct of its affairs;
(2) To meet within 60 days after the receipt of a complaint, to decide if the same is in the proper form and if so to decide whether or not the complaint is unjustified, frivolous, patently unfounded or fails to state facts sufficient to involve the disciplinary jurisdiction of the mayor and council or if further action in a full hearing is necessary;
(3) To prescribe forms, approved by the city attorney, for the disclosures required in this article, and to make available to the public information disclosed as provided in this section;
(4) To receive and hear complaints of violations of the standards required by this article;
(5) To make such investigation and response to a complaint as it deems necessary to determine whether any person has violated any provisions of this article;
(6) To hold such hearings and make such inquiries as deemed necessary to be investigated and rule upon complaints;
(7) To report its findings to the mayor and council for such action as the mayor and council deems appropriate;
(8) To vote on all issues which come before the committee. The chairperson may vote on all issues and not simply to break a tie; and
(9) To meet to hear issues. A quorum shall be constituted by the presence of all three members of the committee; no proxies shall be allowed.
(Ord. of 8-4-2008, § 2-6-8)

